# Response headers for the prerendered pages, which Cloudflare serves straight
# from the CDN without running the worker (see dist/_routes.json). The two
# editor routes bypass this file and get the same headers from
# src/middleware.ts instead.
#
# Deliberately not a Content-Security-Policy. Every reading page carries three
# inline scripts (the pre-paint theme/rail script, the theme toggle, search)
# and loads Google Fonts, so a correct CSP needs per-build hashes regenerated
# whenever those scripts change — a build step and a standing maintenance
# obligation. A CSP that silently breaks the theme toggle after a refactor is
# worse than none. Revisit if the inline scripts ever go away.
#
# These three cannot break a page, which is why they're here and a CSP isn't.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
